course: dictionary
lesson: 14522
title: One word, two jobs: periodical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A periodical is a magazine or journal that comes out regularly, such as every week, every month or every three months. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The school library has a shelf of periodicals about space.» The words library and shelf tell you that periodicals are printed things you can read, not story books.
explain: Periodical can also be an adjective, which describes something. It means happening again and again at regular times. «The nurse made periodical checks on the patient.» The checks come back at set times, not just once, so periodical means repeated at regular times. A shorter form, periodic, means the same thing.
explain: A good test is to swap in a meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. For the noun, try «magazines» in place of «periodicals»: «The school library has a shelf of magazines about space» still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning. For the adjective, try «regular» in place of «periodical»: «regular checks» also fits.
fact: A periodical is a magazine or journal that is published regularly.
fact: «Regularly» can mean every week, every month or every three months.
fact: Periodicals are often kept on special shelves in libraries.
fact: Scientists publish their discoveries in periodicals, so that other scientists can read them.
fact: As an adjective, periodical means happening again and again at regular times, as in «periodical checks».
exercise: «The library has a new periodical about space.» What is a periodical? | *A magazine or journal that comes out regularly | A special shelf for old books | A letter that is sent only once | A book that is finished in one go
exercise: «The bus company does periodical checks on every bus.» What does periodical mean here? | *Happening again and again at regular times | Sent by post | Only once, never again | Very old and broken
exercise: Which of these is a periodical? | *A monthly science magazine, sent to your home every month | A bedtime story you read only once | A single letter from a friend | A monthly science magazine
test: «Scientists share their discoveries in periodicals.» Where do scientists publish their discoveries? | In the playground | Under their beds | *In periodicals, such as science magazines and journals | On the bus to school
test: «The dentist gives periodical checkups every six months.» What does periodical mean in this sentence? | *Happening at regular times | Painful | Only once | Very cheap
exam: Which sentence uses periodical as an adjective? | She put the periodicals back on the library shelf. | The periodicals are kept in the school library. | I read a periodical about frogs every month. | *The nurse made periodical checks on the ward.
